<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,⋮$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nWe could continue the division, but the same digit keeps repeating. Thus, the decimal continues with repeating $6$'s:\n\n$$\n42.166…\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{253}{6}=42.166…=42.1\\overset{―}{6}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551329 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186551195 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551329 #edb/ref 1069 "q-171875" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551329 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551329 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/d2/d29179efa4eaaf77d34a7c044e82c8a6bf053763adf829b83207b652d39fa531.png)\n\nIn the figure above, $m∠B=${{field-1}}${}^{∘}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551329 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bc6c1cea-fda3-5da9-9a26-2a572a4b6650" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551329 #edb/ref 1074 "Since the sum of the measures of the interior angles of a triangle is ${180}^{∘}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{74}^{∘}+(3x+{2}^{∘})+(4x-{1}^{∘}) & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ {75}^{∘}+7x & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 7x & ={105}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={15}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nm∠B=3x+{2}^{∘}=3({15}^{∘})+{2}^{∘}={47}^{∘}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551334 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186551189 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551334 #edb/ref 1069 "q-52490" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551334 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551334 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\sqrt[3]{-{x}^{3}}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551334 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c6c9bca9-ea70-5989-b840-49d437c3ef76" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551334 #edb/ref 1074 "We write the term under the radical as a perfect cube, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{-{x}^{3}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{-x\\cdot x\\cdot x} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{(-x)\\cdot (-x)\\cdot (-x)} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{(-x)^{3}} & = \\\\ -x\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551336 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186551205 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551336 #edb/ref 1069 "q-134560" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551336 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551336 #edb/ref 1071 "$7\\sqrt[3]{21}-3\\sqrt[3]{21}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551336 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d56a0cf9-3169-596f-ae20-a8cf3a250f28" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551336 #edb/ref 1074 "We can combine the two $\\sqrt[3]{21}$ terms together, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7\\sqrt[3]{21}-3\\sqrt[3]{21} & = \\\\ (7-3)\\sqrt[3]{21} & = \\\\ 4\\sqrt[3]{21} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551343 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186551066 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551343 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186551148 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551343 #edb/ref 1069 "q-215134" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551343 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551343 #edb/ref 1071 "Written in **ascending order**, the solutions to $|9-y|=4$ are $y=${{field-1}} and $y=$\n{{field-2}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551343 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "dbb8c729-ab7f-5cd4-a54a-d589b9fc5814" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551343 #edb/ref 1074 "Either the positive or negative of the expression inside the absolute value must be equal to the right-hand side of the equation.\n\nSo, we set up the two corresponding equations and solve them independently:\n\n- If $|9-y|=9-y,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|9-y| & =4 \\\\ 9-y & =4 \\\\ -y & =-5 \\\\ y & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|9-y|=-(9-y),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|9-y| & =4 \\\\ -(9-y) & =4 \\\\ -9+y & =4 \\\\ y & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $y=5$ and $y=13.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551362 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186551462 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551362 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "07b5d5fa-daa3-5f89-8e56-20c3dd4520e0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551362 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186551284 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551373 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186551421 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551373 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2215e19b-c543-5571-819e-bad218c4b156" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551373 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186551334 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551402 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186551471 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551402 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5983725b-bc77-5877-96ff-47136940e09c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551402 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186551254 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551405 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 1759218655141